  <title>6.4.5: Can You Factor the Polynomial?</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01632</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.4.5: Can You Factor the Polynomial?</md:title>
    <md:uuid>84f11b24-d137-4974-b370-0e99555dac97</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>

<title>Student Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which of these polynomials has a greatest common factor of 1? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(10q^2 + 14q + 20\) </item>
  <item> \(12x^3 − 2x\) </item>
  <item> \(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\) </item>
  <item> \(−2x − 4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>  \(12x^3y − 7g^8h^3 + 11s^2\)</para>
<para>Determine if the expression can be factored by grouping. If it can, factor the expression. If not, answer “prime.”</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(cd + 6c + 4d + 24\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((d + 6)(c + 4)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 − y + 4w − 3\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> prime</para></section>
</content>
